{"step_index":327,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T07:15:30Z","thinking":"**Investigating Demo Payment Failure**\n\nI'm digging into why the demo payment simulation failed. The screenshot shows a \"Not Found\" error after a simulated successful EcoCash payment on Vercel. My immediate focus is `/api/demo-payment` - it seems like that endpoint is the culprit. I need to figure out why it returned a 404.\n\n\n**Analyzing Vercel Configuration**\n\nI've been examining the Vercel configuration file, `vercel.json`. The rewrite rules there, specifically the one targeting `/api/(.*)`, seem crucial. It appears Vercel is automatically deploying `api/index.py` as a serverless function at `/api`. This is likely where the error originates. Now I need to figure out how FastAPI handles the rewritten path. I'm focusing on the `scope[\"path\"]` variable to see if this is being passed into `api/index.py` correctly.\n\n\n**Clarifying Endpoint Routing**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the endpoint routing and how Vercel handles it with FastAPI. The `scope[\"path\"]` is either `/demo-payment` or `/demo-payment`. I'm verifying the Vercel routing, and how that interacts with the `app.py` definitions of `/api/demo-payment` and `/demo-payment`. Specifically, I am clarifying whether Vercel is looking for a separate `api/demo-payment.py` file, or if it correctly uses the `/api/index.py` from the rewrite rule. Finally, I'll test routing by changing the post requests.\n\n\n**Verifying API Endpoint Routing**\n\nI'm now focusing on how the `/api/demo-payment` call from `checkout.html` is routed. I'm verifying the `vercel.json` rewrite rule's configuration, comparing the possibilities: `/api/index.py`, or `/api`, and confirming this against Vercel's official FastAPI documentation. Also, I'm analyzing the fallback logic in `checkout.html`, which retries the call to `/demo-payment` if the `/api/demo-payment` call returns a 404, both of which are defined in `app.py`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"{\\n  \\\"rewrites\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"/checkout\\\",\\n      \\\"destination\\\": \\\"/checkout.html\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"/library\\\",\\n      \\\"destination\\\": \\\"/library.html\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"/api/(.*)\\\",\\n      \\\"destination\\\": \\\"/api/index.py\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"/(demo-payment|session|media|play-events|health)(.*)\\\",\\n      \\\"destination\\\": \\\"/api/index.py\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"/docs\\\",\\n      \\\"destination\\\": \\\"/api/index.py\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"/redoc\\\",\\n      \\\"destination\\\": \\\"/api/index.py\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"/openapi.json\\\",\\n      \\\"destination\\\": \\\"/api/index.py\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"","Description":"\"Update vercel.json rewrites to route both /api/* and root API endpoints to api/index.py\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\dell\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\\\vercel.json\"","toolAction":"\"Updating vercel.json with fail-safe rewrites\"","toolSummary":"\"Updating vercel.json with fail-safe rewrites\""}}]}
