{"step_index":359,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T07:29:33Z","thinking":"**Investigating Vercel Routing**\n\nI'm hitting a roadblock. Both `/health` and `/api/health` are returning 404s, which strongly suggests Vercel isn't even attempting to route requests to `api/index.py`. The focus has shifted to understanding Vercel's zero-config Python build rules to pinpoint why this function isn't being invoked.\n\n\n**Clarifying Vercel's Build Rules**\n\nI've made a breakthrough. I'm now certain that Vercel requires either a `requirements.txt` file or explicit `builds` configuration within `vercel.json` to recognize Python serverless functions like `api/index.py`. The crucial missing piece was understanding how Vercel identifies and handles Python projects without a build configuration.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"{\\n  \\\"builds\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"api/index.py\\\",\\n      \\\"use\\\": \\\"@vercel/python\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"routes\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/api/(.*)\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"/api/index.py\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/checkout\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"/checkout.html\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/library\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"/library.html\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/(.*)\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"/$1\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"","Description":"\"Update vercel.json to build api/index.py as @vercel/python function and route /api/* to it\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\dell\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\\\vercel.json\"","toolAction":"\"Updating vercel.json with builds configuration\"","toolSummary":"\"Updating vercel.json with builds configuration\""}}]}
