{"step_index":365,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T07:33:29Z","thinking":"**Analyzing the Error**\n\nOkay, I'm now zeroing in on this 404 error from that screenshot. The server, streamwave-gamma.vercel.app, is returning a \"NOT_FOUND\" response. The code and ID are also showing as NOT_FOUND. I'm trying to figure out the root cause. My focus is now on what specific resource that server might be failing to deliver.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Root Cause**\n\nI've discovered the root cause of the 404 error! The problem stems from the explicit `builds` configuration in `vercel.json`. By specifying only the Python file and *not* including static files in the `builds` section, Vercel disables its automatic static file detection for the root path (`/`). Now I see why `/` was not serving `index.html`. It appears Vercel's behavior changed, and the old config is no longer valid.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\dell\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\\\api\\\\index.py\"","EndLine":"15","StartLine":"1","toolAction":"\"Viewing api/index.py\"","toolSummary":"\"Viewing api/index.py\""}}]}
